2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  CLAIM    no polling timer, no dedup, and a badge failure discards a good list
2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  ROOT     Three separate defects in one delivery path. (1) Zero QTimer: nothing polled, so unreadCountChanged only fired when a view called refresh(). (2) Delivery was paired: handleRefreshReply stored each half into pendingResponse_/pendingBadge_ and required `refreshPending_ == 0 && pendingBadge_` before applying anything. (3) failRefresh bumped refreshGeneration_, which made the sibling reply's generation check fail, and cleared both pending slots -- so ONE 404 discarded the other half's data, and the discarded half was the list, not the counter.
2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  CHANGE   src/suno/SunoNotificationService.{hpp,cpp}: constructor takes pollIntervalMs (default 60000, 0 disables) and starts one QTimer whose slot returns early when signed out, loading or marking read. Each reply is applied on arrival: the list assigns notifications_ and emits notificationsChanged only when the RAW BODY differs from the last applied one (dedup, so a poll cannot rebuild the list under a scroll position); the badge updates unreadCount_ and emits only on change. refreshPending_ now only decides when loading ends. failRefresh decrements the outstanding count and reports the error without touching the generation or the other half.
2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  TEST     tests/unit/suno/test_SunoNotificationService.cpp gains a ScriptedReply + fakeBearer harness (the suite previously only tested the static parsers and had no QCoreApplication, which the delivery cases need) and three cases: aBadgeFailureDoesNotDiscardTheList (list 1 notification, badge 404 -> notificationsChanged once, size 1, error non-empty, not loading), anUnchangedListIsAppliedOnce (same body twice -> exactly one emit), pollingRefreshesWithoutAView (signed-out service issues no request in 120 ms; an authenticated one with a 10 ms interval reaches >= 4 list requests).
2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  VERIFY   ./build.sh --fast --tests -> exit 0.
2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  VERIFY   ctest --test-dir build-fast/tests -R '^test_SunoNotificationService$' --output-on-failure -> Passed 11.45 s; the three new cases pass individually (direct run: 9 passed, 0 failed).
2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  VERIFY   ctest --test-dir build-fast/tests --output-on-failure -j3 -> 100% tests passed, 0 failed out of 14 (141.44 s).
2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  NOTE     The suite's wall time went from ~1 s to ~11 s because each case drives a real SunoClient through its rate-limited request queue. That is the cost of testing the delivery path instead of the parser, and it is the only entry whose time moved.
2026-10-23T20:40:00Z  NOT-VERIFIED  That a 60 s poll is the right cadence for a real account, and that the badge value the server reports matches what the UI should show: both need MT-001 with a live session.
